---
import MainLayout from '../../layouts/MainLayout.astro';

// Held as a string: a bare `{` in .astro markup opens a JS expression, so this
// JSON was compiled as JavaScript and broke the build.
const vscodeSettings = `{
  "editor.formatOnSave": true,
  "editor.defaultFormatter": "esbenp.prettier-vscode",
  "editor.rulers": [80, 100],
  "files.exclude": {
    "**/.DS_Store": true,
    "**/node_modules": true
  }
}`;
---

<MainLayout title="Developer Setup | Salesdam Docs" description="Development environment setup guide">
  <div class="content-wrapper">
    <h1>Developer Setup</h1>

    <p class="intro">Complete guide to setting up your development environment for Salesdam.</p>

    <h2>Prerequisites</h2>

    <p>Before you begin, ensure you have:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Node.js 16+ (check with `node --version`)</li>
      <li>npm 7+ or yarn 1.22+ (check with `npm --version`)</li>
      <li>Git (check with `git --version`)</li>
      <li>MongoDB 4.4+ running locally or Atlas account</li>
      <li>Code editor (VS Code recommended)</li>
      <li>Terminal/Command line experience</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>System Requirements</h2>

    <table>
      <tr>
        <th>Component</th>
        <th>Minimum</th>
        <th>Recommended</th>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Node.js</td>
        <td>14.0</td>
        <td>18.0+</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>npm</td>
        <td>6.0</td>
        <td>9.0+</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>RAM</td>
        <td>4GB</td>
        <td>8GB</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Disk Space</td>
        <td>2GB</td>
        <td>5GB</td>
      </tr>
    </table>

    <h2>Installation Steps</h2>

    <h3>1. Install Node.js</h3>

    <p>Download and install from <a href="https://nodejs.org">nodejs.org</a></p>

    <p>Verify installation:</p>
    <pre><code>node --version
npm --version</code></pre>

    <h3>2. Install MongoDB</h3>

    <p><strong>Option A: Local Installation</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Download from <a href="https://www.mongodb.com/try/download/community">mongodb.com</a></li>
      <li>Follow installation guide for your OS</li>
      <li>Start MongoDB service</li>
    </ul>

    <p><strong>Option B: MongoDB Atlas (Cloud)</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Create account at <a href="https://www.mongodb.com/cloud/atlas">mongodb.com/cloud/atlas</a></li>
      <li>Create a free cluster</li>
      <li>Get connection string</li>
    </ul>

    <p>Verify MongoDB:</p>
    <pre><code>mongosh
# Should connect to MongoDB shell</code></pre>

    <h3>3. Clone Repository</h3>

    <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/your-org/salesdam-v3.git
cd salesdam-v3</code></pre>

    <h3>4. Install Dependencies</h3>

    <p><strong>Backend:</strong></p>
    <pre><code>cd backend
npm install</code></pre>

    <p><strong>Frontend:</strong></p>
    <pre><code>cd ../frontend
npm install</code></pre>

    <p><strong>Docs:</strong></p>
    <pre><code>cd ../docs
npm install</code></pre>

    <h2>Environment Configuration</h2>

    <h3>Backend .env Setup</h3>

    <p>Create `.env` file in backend folder:</p>

    <pre><code># Database
MONGO_URI=mongodb://localhost:27017/salesdam

# Server
PORT=5000
NODE_ENV=development

# Sessions — an opaque id in a cookie, stored in MongoDB; no secret needed
SESSION_MAX_AGE=86400000

# CORS — the frontend dev server origin (see frontend/vite.config.js)
CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173,http://localhost:5174

# SMTP (Email)
SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
SMTP_PORT=587
SMTP_USER=your_email@gmail.com
SMTP_PASS=your_app_password
SMTP_FROM=noreply@salesdam.com

# Application
APP_URL=http://localhost:5173
API_URL=http://localhost:5000</code></pre>

    <h3>Frontend .env Setup</h3>

    <p>Create `.env` file in frontend folder:</p>

    <pre><code># API Configuration — the origin only; the app appends /api/v1
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:5000</code></pre>

    <h2>Running Development Servers</h2>

    <p>Start three terminal windows:</p>

    <h3>Terminal 1: Backend</h3>
    <pre><code>cd backend
npm run dev</code></pre>
    <p>Runs on http://localhost:5000</p>

    <h3>Terminal 2: Frontend</h3>
    <pre><code>cd frontend
npm run dev</code></pre>
    <p>Runs on http://localhost:5173</p>

    <h3>Terminal 3: Docs</h3>
    <pre><code>cd docs
npm run dev</code></pre>
    <p>Runs on http://localhost:4321 (or next available port)</p>

    <h2>Verify Setup</h2>

    <p>Check that everything is working:</p>

    <ol>
      <li>✓ MongoDB is running</li>
      <li>✓ Backend server starts without errors</li>
      <li>✓ Frontend loads at http://localhost:5173</li>
      <li>✓ Can create a new account</li>
      <li>✓ Can login and see dashboard</li>
      <li>✓ Can access docs at http://localhost:4321</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>IDE Setup (VS Code)</h2>

    <p>Recommended extensions:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>ES7+ React/Redux/React-Native snippets</li>
      <li>Prettier - Code formatter</li>
      <li>ESLint</li>
      <li>MongoDB for VS Code</li>
      <li>Thunder Client or REST Client</li>
    </ul>

    <p>Add `.vscode/settings.json`:</p>
    <pre><code>{vscodeSettings}</code></pre>

    <h2>Common Issues</h2>

    <h3>MongoDB Connection Error</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Ensure MongoDB is running</li>
      <li>Check connection string in .env</li>
      <li>Verify database credentials</li>
      <li>Check firewall settings</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Port Already in Use</h3>
    <pre><code># Find and kill process using port 5000
lsof -i :5000
kill -9 [PID]

# Or use different port
PORT=5001 npm run dev</code></pre>

    <h3>npm Install Fails</h3>
    <pre><code># Clear npm cache
npm cache clean --force

# Delete node_modules and package-lock.json
rm -rf node_modules package-lock.json

# Reinstall
npm install</code></pre>

    <h2>Next Steps</h2>

    <ul>
      <li><a href="/developer/backend">Backend Development Guide</a></li>
      <li><a href="/developer/frontend">Frontend Development Guide</a></li>
      <li><a href="/api/overview">API Documentation</a></li>
    </ul>

    <div class="success">
      <strong>✓ Ready!</strong> Your development environment is set up. Start coding!
    </div>
  </div>
</MainLayout>
